The coordinates and hover pixel has been removed on mobile as it doesn't make sense to include this for touchscreens without a cursor. Previously the hover pixel would stay around when moving about the canvas even though there is no cursor.

I determined that the latest version of Safari on iOS 16 allows for the canvas size to be increased without crashing. I increased the scale level on iOS to 10x which is enough to make the pixels reasonably crisp whilst maintaining reasonable performance and reducing possibility of crashes. I reduced the scaling for desktop Safari from 30x to 20x which should improve performance slightly whilst keeping the pixels reasonably crisp as seen with my own testing.

@Sentinelrv If you are able to test at some point with iOS 16, that would be great. However, I have already tested it and it works well.

