### About:

In this pull request I've extracted the "stack installation" related codes to their own corresponding class.

These are not breaking-changes so in case it's approves, it should work without any problems.

### Core changes:

- [x] Extracted installation helpers from the [`InstallCommand`](https://github.com/OzanKurt/breeze/blob/dba3ef2368cc616075fabca59086c60b99ae69b3/src/Console/InstallCommand.php) to an [`AbstractInstaller`](https://github.com/OzanKurt/breeze/blob/dba3ef2368cc616075fabca59086c60b99ae69b3/src/Installers/AbstractInstaller.php) class.
- [x] Previous stacks are extracted to their own installer classes:
    - [`ApiStack`](https://github.com/OzanKurt/breeze/blob/dba3ef2368cc616075fabca59086c60b99ae69b3/src/Installers/ApiStack.php)
    - [`BladeStack`](https://github.com/OzanKurt/breeze/blob/dba3ef2368cc616075fabca59086c60b99ae69b3/src/Installers/BladeStack.php)
    - [`InertiaReactStack`](https://github.com/OzanKurt/breeze/blob/dba3ef2368cc616075fabca59086c60b99ae69b3/src/Installers/InertiaReactStack.php)
    - [`InertiaVueStack`](https://github.com/OzanKurt/breeze/blob/dba3ef2368cc616075fabca59086c60b99ae69b3/src/Installers/InertiaVueStack.php)
- [x] [`InstallCommand`](https://github.com/OzanKurt/breeze/blob/dba3ef2368cc616075fabca59086c60b99ae69b3/src/Console/InstallCommand.php) will now only handle which stack to install and print an error message in case the entered stack is invalid.
- [x] Added a [`config/breeze.php`](https://github.com/OzanKurt/breeze/blob/dba3ef2368cc616075fabca59086c60b99ae69b3/config/breeze.php) which allows users to add their custom `Installer` class.

```php
use Laravel\Breeze\Installers\ApiStack;
use Laravel\Breeze\Installers\BladeStack;
use Laravel\Breeze\Installers\InertiaVueStack;
use Laravel\Breeze\Installers\InertiaReactStack;

return [
    'stacks' => [
        'vue' => InertiaVueStack::class,
        'react' => InertiaReactStack::class,
        'blade' => BladeStack::class,
        'api' => ApiStack::class,
    ],
];
```


### Here is an example of a custom stack installer:

1- Run the `php artisan vendor:publish --tag=breeze-config` command to publish the default config file.
2- Add your custom stack to the config file.

```php
// ...
use App\Services\Breeze\Stacks\CustomStack;

return [
    'stacks' => [
        // ...
        'custom' => CustomStack::class,
    ],
];
```
3- Create the `CustomStack` installer and extend the `AbstractInstaller`, remember that you have access to all the method from the `AbstractInstaller`.
```php
<?php

namespace App\Services\Breeze\Stacks;

use Illuminate\Filesystem\Filesystem;
use Laravel\Breeze\Contracts\StackInstaller;
use Laravel\Breeze\Installers\AbstractInstaller;

class CustomStack extends AbstractInstaller implements StackInstaller
{
    public function install(): void
    {
        // Install a custom stack...
    }
}
```
